1.214.m:
Sumantu said:
Padminī, and likewise another is Madhyamā, then Anāmanī,
Arkiṇī, Jvālinī, Tejanī, and Gabhastinī;

1.216.m:
In front of the śūdras the vaiśyas [should sit], and in front of the vaiśyas the kṣatriyas;
situated in the middle of all of them, the reciter should speak, O king;
and those men who are born of mixed unions, O king, [should sit] behind the śūdras.
